    "afterword": "<h3>Summer Minor</h3><p><strong>This 5-course sequence comprises a Summer Minor in Electrochemical Science, Engineering, and Technology  (approved for 2026).  This is the first of its kind in the Nation.</strong></p><p><a href=\"https://summer.berkeley.edu/special-programs/summer-minors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://summer.berkeley.edu/special-programs/summer-minors</a></p><p>Questions: <a href=\"mailto:electrochemistry@berkeley.edu\">electrochemistry@berkeley.edu</a> </p><p><a href=\"https://undergraduate.catalog.berkeley.edu/programs/10I178U\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong><em>Electrochemistry Science, Engineering, and Technology</em> Summer Minor</strong></a></p><h3>Laboratory and Project Materials Fee</h3><p>Courses with laboratory and project components include a $300 laboratory and project materials fee. This fee helps cover the direct costs of hands-on electrochemistry instruction, including consumable supplies, electrodes, electrochemical cells and fixtures, chemicals, membranes and other project-specific materials. It also supports shared use, repair, calibration, and maintenance of research-grade laboratory equipment needed for electrochemical measurements, cell assembly, and device testing.</p><p>The fee is used to ensure that students can work with practical electrochemical systems and complete laboratory or research-style projects using appropriate materials and instrumentation. It is separate from tuition and directly supports the additional costs associated with project-based experimental instruction central to key experiential learning included in these courses.</p><p><em>Berkeley Summer Sessions is open to a wide variety of students, including UC Berkeley degree-seeking students, students from other UC campuses, visiting students from around the U.S. and the world as well as the general public.</em></p>"
